+# Audit categories
+
+Categories, not patterns. A new pattern lands under an existing category. "Covered by" names the
+control in this project; the last column says whether a test asserts it.
+
+| Category | Covered by | Enforced mechanically? |
+|---|---|---|
+| Authentication and sessions | `authenticated` before_action in `app/controllers/application_controller.rb`; `current_user` resolved from the `auth_token` cookie or the session | partly: the feature specs sign in |
+| Authorization per route | `administrative` filter in `app/controllers/application_controller.rb`, applied per controller | no |
+| Ownership of rows | `has_one` and `has_many` associations on `User` (`app/models/user.rb`), used through `current_user` | yes for messages (`spec/guards/message_scoping_spec.rb`); no for the rest |
+| Input validation | strong parameters declared per controller | no |
+| File handling | extension allow-list and size cap in `app/controllers/benefit_forms_controller.rb` | no |
